{"resource":{"id":"computer-networks-interview-questions","title":"Computer Networks \u2014 Interview Questions","category":"CS Core","difficulty":"Intermediate","readingTime":"43 min","pages":47,"lastUpdated":"July 2026","tags":["Networks","TCP/IP","CS Core"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"350+ Computer Networks interview questions \u2014 beginner to senior, with layered hints, detailed answers, design questions, TCP/IP, routing, switching, troubleshooting, HR, and mocks."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"intro","label":"Introduction"},{"id":"basics","label":"Basics (80 Qs)"},{"id":"ip","label":"IP & Subnetting (60 Qs)"},{"id":"routing","label":"Routing (60 Qs)"},{"id":"switching","label":"Switching (50 Qs)"},{"id":"proto","label":"Protocols (50 Qs)"},{"id":"design","label":"Network Design (30 Qs)"},{"id":"trouble","label":"Troubleshooting Scenarios (20 Qs)"},{"id":"hr","label":"HR & Behavioral"},{"id":"mocks","label":"Mock Interviews"},{"id":"compare","label":"Comparison Table"},{"id":"commands","label":"Commands & Code Reference"},{"id":"best","label":"Best Practices & Tips"},{"id":"mistakes","label":"Common Mistakes"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary & Key Takeaways"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQs"},{"id":"references","label":"Further Reading & References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Computer Networks \u2014 Complete Tutorial","tag":"CS Core","time":"47 min"},{"title":"Computer Networks \u2014 Cheat Sheet","tag":"CS Core","time":"5 min"},{"title":"Computer Networks \u2014 Interview Questions","tag":"CS Core","time":"43 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Master the core ideas covered in this resource.</li>\n          <li>Apply concepts to hands-on labs and real networks.</li>\n          <li>Ready you for interviews and certifications.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"intro\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Introduction</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>350+ Computer Networks interview questions \u2014 beginner to senior, with layered hints, detailed answers, design questions, TCP/IP, routing, switching, troubleshooting, HR, and mocks.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 \u2014 Overview illustration for Computer Networks \u2014 Interview Questions.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"basics\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Basics (80 Qs)</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>What is OSI? TCP vs UDP? Difference between hub, switch, router? What is DHCP? What is DNS?</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ip\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">IP &amp; Subnetting (60 Qs)</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Given 192.168.1.0/26, how many hosts? Design a subnet for 5 departments.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 \u2014 Reference diagram for ip & subnetting (60 qs).\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"routing\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Routing (60 Qs)</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>OSPF vs BGP? Convergence? Admin distance? Route redistribution pitfalls?</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"switching\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Switching (50 Qs)</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>STP states? Root bridge election? Trunk vs access? VLAN hopping mitigations?</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"proto\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Protocols (50 Qs)</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>3-way handshake in detail. Slow start. Fast retransmit. UDP use cases.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"design\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Network Design (30 Qs)</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Design a network for a 3-floor office. Redundancy plan. IP scheme. WAN options.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"trouble\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Troubleshooting Scenarios (20 Qs)</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>User can't reach internet \u2014 walk through your steps. Intermittent packet loss \u2014 how to isolate?</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"hr\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">HR &amp; Behavioral</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Tell me about a network you designed. A time you led an incident response.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"mocks\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Mock Interviews</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Two 45-min mocks with rubric and scoring guide.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"compare\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Comparison Table</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Aspect</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">TCP</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">UDP</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Reliability</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Guaranteed</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Best-effort</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Ordering</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Yes</td><td class=\"border p-2\">No</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Overhead</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Higher</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Lower</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Use cases</td><td class=\"border p-2\">HTTP, SSH, email</td><td class=\"border p-2\">DNS, VoIP, gaming</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 \u2014 Protocol behavior at a glance.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"commands\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Commands &amp; Code Reference</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>! Cisco IOS \u2014 VLAN + trunk basics\nvlan 10\n name USERS\nvlan 20\n name VOICE\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/1\n switchport mode access\n switchport access vlan 10\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/24\n switchport mode trunk\n switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"best\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Best Practices &amp; Tips</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Baseline before you optimize.</li>\n          <li>Document intent, not just configs.</li>\n          <li>Automate repetitive changes.</li>\n          <li>Segment aggressively; deny by default.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"mistakes\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Common Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Overlapping subnets across sites.</li>\n          <li>Trunks allowing all VLANs.</li>\n          <li>Skipping change reviews.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Layered thinking, clean IP planning, and disciplined operations turn a network from fragile to boring \u2014 in the best way.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>How is this different from a general IT course?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">This resource focuses purely on networking concepts and their application.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Do I need Cisco hardware?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No \u2014 Packet Tracer and GNS3 emulate everything you need.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is content current?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes \u2014 reflects modern protocols and enterprise practices as of July 2026.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Further Reading &amp; References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Educational content. Vendor commands and versions may change \u2014 always verify against current documentation.</p>\n    